 "あまり": "بَقِيَّة (A part or parts remaining after some has/have been removed or already occurred.)  [remainder]\nمثال: ぎょうざの具のあまりは？餃子を家で作りましたが、皮が少なかったせいか、具が少し余ってしまいました。\n→ Gyoza stuffing? I made some gyoza at home but, possibly because I didn't have enough dough, I had some of the filling left over. / جِدًّا (To a great extent or degree.)  [(not) very]\nwith neg. sentence\nمثال: それはあまり価値がない。\n→ It's not worth much. / [too much ; excessively]\nesp. as あまりに(も) / الْأُقْصَى, الْأَبْعَد (Of a place, the most remote, farthest or outermost.) / شَدِيد (In the greatest or highest degree; intense.) / غَيْر اِعْتِيَادِيّ (Excessive, or far beyond the norm.) / خَطِير (Drastic, or of great severity.) / مُتَطَرِّف (Of sports, difficult or dangerous; performed in a hazardous environment.) / أَخِير (Ultimate, final or last.)  [extreme]\nمثال: スイートルームのあまりの豪華さにウットリした。\n→ We were entranced by the fabulous suite.",
 "あまりに": "أَيْضًا, كَذٰلِكَ (Likewise.) / أَكْثَرَ مِنَ اللّازِمِ, لِلْغايةِ (To an excessive degree, more than enough indicates that the degree of a quality )  [too (much)]\nمثال: 料理にあまりに時間がかかりすぎる。\n→ Cooking takes up too much time.",
