 "ありがたさ": "قِيمَة (The quality that renders something desirable or valuable; worth.)  [value]\nمثال: 水不足の時、水のありがたさを骨身にしみて感じた。\n→ During the water shortage, the value of water really came home to me.",
 "ありがたみ": "قِيمَة (The quality that renders something desirable or valuable; worth.)  [value]\nمثال: 随分尽くしてやったのに、それでも彼にはありがたみが無かった。\n→ After all we had done, he was still ungrateful.",
 "ありがたや": "الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ (Expression of relief or gratitude.)  [thank goodness]",
 "ありがち": "شَائِع (Found in large numbers or in a large quantity; usual.) / شَائِع (Simple, ordinary or vulgar.)  [common]\nمثال: 今度の上司？個性的どころか、ありがちなタイプね。\n→ The new supervisor? He's not very original - pretty much like the rest.",
 "ありがと": "شُكْرًا, شُكْرًا (An expression of gratitude or politeness in response to something done or given.)  [thank you]\nمثال: ご読了ありがとございました〜。\n→ Thank you for reading to the end.",
 "ありがとう": "شُكْرًا, شُكْرًا (An expression of gratitude or politeness in response to something done or given.)  [thank you]\nمثال: ありがとう。また、次の日にくるようにします。\n→ Thanks. Maybe we'll come back.",
 "ありがとうございました": "شُكْرًا, شُكْرًا (An expression of gratitude or politeness in response to something done or given.)  [thank you]\nused for past actions",
 "ありがとうございます": "شُكْرًا, شُكْرًا (An expression of gratitude or politeness in response to something done or given.)  [thank you]\nمثال: 親切なお手紙をいただきありがとうございます。\n→ I appreciate your kind letter.",
 "ありがとうさん": "شُكْرًا, شُكْرًا (An expression of gratitude or politeness in response to something done or given.)  [thank you]",
