 "いくせいぎゅう": "عِجْل (A young cow or bull of any bovid, such as domestic cattle or buffalo.) / دَغْفَل, حُوَار (The young of various animals, especially elephant, giraffe, reindeer, seal, or w) / بَطَّة, رَبْلَةُ (The back of the leg below the knee.) / بَطْن اَلسَّاق (The muscle in the back of the leg below the knee.)  [calf]",
 "いくせん": "أَلْف, ١٠٠٠ (A numerical value equal to 1,000; ten times a hundred (1 E+3 exactly—in scientif)  [thousands]\nمثال: 一人の個人の中に幾千ものことなった人間がいる。\n→ Within every man are thousands.",
 "いくた": "كَثِير (before a countable noun: A large, indefinite number of.) / كَثِير, متعدد (A large, indefinite number of people or things.)  [many]\nمثال: 我々は幾多の困難を克服しなければならない。\n→ We have to cope with hosts of difficulties.",
 "いくたび": "كَثِيرًا, غَالِبًا (Frequently; many times on different occasions.)  [(how) often]\nمثال: 今日の幸せが幾度も巡ってきますように。\n→ Many happy returns of the day! Happy birthday!",
 "いくちよ": "عُمْر (The amount of time that some being has been alive, or that some thing has been i) / سِنّ (Any particular stage of life.)  [ages]",
 "いくつ": "كَم / كَمْ (what number)  [how many]\nمثال: いいえ、おもちゃがいくつあるかじゃなくて、鍵がいくつあるかなのよ。\n→ No, not how many toys, how many keys? / [how old]\nمثال: あなたのお父さんはおいくつですか。\n→ How old is your father?",
 "いくつか": "قَلِيل (An indefinite, but usually small, number of.) / قَلِيل (Not many; a small (in comparison with another number stated or implied) but some) / قَلِيل (Few people, few things.)  [(a) few]\nمثال: いくつかの点で私は彼女が気に入らない。\n→ I don't like her in some ways.",
