 "いくひさしく": "إِلَى الْأَبَد (For all time, for all eternity; for a lifetime; for an infinite amount of time.)  [forever]\nin formal correspondence or greetings",
 "いくぶん": "[somewhat ; to some extent]\nمثال: この問題は私にとっては幾分難しい。\n→ This problem is difficult for me to some degree. / بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some]\nمثال: そのケーキは幾分レモンの味がした。\n→ There was some taste of lemon in the cake.",
 "いくぶんか": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some] / [somewhat ; to some extent]",
