 "いけすかない": "مُقْرِف, مُقَزِّز (Causing disgust; repulsive; distasteful.)  [disgusting]\nمثال: 自分と気があわない、いけ好かない、人がいるとします。\n→ Suppose there's some jerk you just can't get on with.",
 "いけず": "عَنَى, عَنَى (To convey (a meaning).) / لَئِيم, خَسِيس (Intending to cause harm, successfully or otherwise; bearing ill will towards ano) / مُتَوَسِّط (the statistical value)  [mean]",
 "いけずうずうしい": "وَقِح, صَفِيق (Having no shame, no guilt nor remorse over something considered wrong; immodest,)  [shameless]",
 "いけぞんざい": "فَظّ (Lacking in refinement or civility; bad-mannered; discourteous.)  [rude]",
 "いけてる": "بَارِد (Of a mildly low temperature.) / يُبَرِّد (To lose heat, to get colder.)  [cool]\nمثال: 「それよりそのカッコ・・・水着！？」「そうよ。イケてるでしょー！？ムラムラする〜？」\n→ \"Never mind that, what's with that get up ... a swimming suit!?\" \"That's right. Sexy isn't it? Feeling horny?\"",
 "いけない": "سَيِّئ, وحش (Good, superlative, excellent, cool.)  [bad] / [must not (do, be) ; should not]\nafter the -te form of a verb or adjective\nمثال: このフロッピーをフォーマットしてはいけません。\n→ You mustn't format this floppy disk. / عَدِيمُ الْفَائِدَةِ (Without use or the possibility to be used.)  [useless]\nمثال: 彼本人は好人物なんだが、その取り巻きがどうもいけないね。\n→ I really like him, but not his circle of friends. / [hopeless ; beyond hope]",
 "いけにえ": "تَضْحِيَة, قُرْبَان (A human being or an animal, or a physical object or immaterial thing (see etymol) / ضَحَّى ((transitive) to offer (a human being or an animal, or an obj)  [(living) sacrifice] / ضَحِيَّة (one who is harmed) / أُضْحِيَّة (a living being slain and offered as a sacrifice)  [victim]\nمثال: タランチュラはそのいけにえを素早く捕まえた。\n→ The tarantula seized its victim very quickly.",
 "いけばな": "إِيكِيبَانَا (The Japanese art of flower arrangement.)  [ikebana]\nمثال: 生け花は日本では伝統的な芸道である。\n→ Flower arrangement is a traditional art in Japan.",
 "いけません": "مُخْطِئ (Asserting something incorrect or untrue.) / ظَلَمَ (To treat unjustly; to injure or harm; to do wrong by.)  [wrong] / [hopeless ; past hope] / [must not do] / [cannot go]",
 "いける": "رَتَّبَ (To set up; to organize; to put into an orderly sequence or arrangement.)  [to arrange (flowers)]\nمثال: 彼女は花を生けるのが好きです。\n→ She likes to arrange flowers. / حَيّ (Having life; alive.) / مَعِيشَة, مَعَاش (Financial means; a means of maintaining life; livelihood) / حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of life.)  [living]",
 "いけるくち": "شَارِب (Agent noun of drink; someone or something that drinks.)  [drinker]",
 "いける口": "شَارِب (Agent noun of drink; someone or something that drinks.)  [drinker]",
