 "いつぞや": "مُنْذُ بِضْعَةْ أَيَّام, بِالْأَمْس (Recently; lately; a few days ago.)  [the other day]",
 "いつだって": "دَائِمًا, أَبَدًا (At all times; throughout all time; since the beginning.)  [always]\nمثال: いつだって読書の時間は見つけられる。\n→ We can always find time for reading.",
 "いつだつ": "إِنْحِرَاف (The act of deviating; wandering off the correct or true path or road.)  [deviation] / إِغْفَال (The act of omitting.)  [(accidental) omission]",
 "いつつ": "خَمْسَة, خمسة (A numerical value equal to 5; the number following four and preceding six.)  [five]\nمثال: この箱にはリンゴが五つ入っている。\n→ This box contains five apples. / [five years of age] / اَلسَّاعَة اَلثَّامِنَة (The start of the ninth hour of the day; 8:00 a.m. (08:00).)  [eight o'clock (old time system)]",
