 "いまだかつて": "أَبَدًا (At no time; on no occasion; in no circumstance.)  [never (before)]\nwith neg. sentence\nمثال: そんなものは未だかつて見たことがない。\n→ Never have I seen such a thing.",
 "いまだに": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nindic. surprise or annoyance\nمثال: 彼はいまだに古い車を愛用している。\n→ He still cherishes his old car.",
 "いまっぽい": "عَصْرِيّ, حَدِيث (Pertaining to a current or recent time and style; not ancient.)  [modern]",
 "いまでこそ": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now (unlike then)]\nusu. as 今でこそ...だが...",
 "いまでは": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now]",
 "いまでも": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nمثال: 私は今でも彼女の名を覚えている。\n→ I still bear her name in mind.",
 "いまとなっては": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now]",
 "いまどき": "الْيَوْمَ, النهارده (On the current day or date.) / حَاضِر, الأيام دي (In the current era; nowadays; these days.) / الْيَوْم (today (noun)) / النهرده (today (noun)) / اليوم (today (noun)) / اليوم (today (noun)) / هاد النهار (today (noun))  [today]\nمثال: いまどきそんなことは子供だってしないだろう。\n→ A child today would not do that. / [at this time (of day) ; at this hour]",
 "いまなお": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]",
 "いまにして": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [(only) now (doing, occurring, etc.)]\nesp. 今にして思えば",
 "いまになって": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [(only) now]\nمثال: 長いこと贅沢三昧に暮らしていた彼らが、今になって何もない質素な生活に耐えるなんてとても無理な話だ。\n→ They lived high on the hog for so long, and now they can't adjust to a simple life without luxuries.",
 "いまのうち": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now (while the time is ripe)]\nusu. ～に\nمثال: 今のうちにそれをしなさい。\n→ Do it when you have time.",
 "いまのとこ": "حَالِيًّا (At this moment, at present, now.)  [currently]",
 "いまのところ": "حَالِيًّا (At this moment, at present, now.)  [currently]\nمثال: 今のところお金はいらない。\n→ I don't need money at present.",
 "いまはこれまで": "وَاجِب (Impossible to avoid; bound to happen.)  [unavoidable]",
 "いまはなき": "غَادَرَ, رَحَلَ (To leave.)  [departed]",
 "いまはむかし": "كَان يَامَا كَان (A long time ago; at some time in the past (a traditional beginning of children's)  [once upon a time]",
 "いまは昔": "كَان يَامَا كَان (A long time ago; at some time in the past (a traditional beginning of children's)  [once upon a time]",
 "いまひとつ": "آخَر, إِضَافِيّ (One more further, in addition to the quantity by then; a second or additional on) / آخَر, أُخْرَى (Not the same; different.)  [another (one)] / كَافٍ (sufficient) / تَمَامًا (Sufficiently.) / مَه, كَفَى (Stop! Don't do that any more! It is too much!)  [(not) enough]\nمثال: 新しい車の調子がいま一つです。操縦がきかない。\n→ I had trouble with the new car. It was difficult to steer.",
 "いまふう": "عَصْرِيّ, حَدِيث (Pertaining to a current or recent time and style; not ancient.)  [modern]",
 "いまほど": "[as (much as) it is now ; as much as the present]\nusu. with negative sentence\nمثال: 学生時代は彼は今ほど優しくなかった。\n→ In his school days he wasn't as gentle as he is now. / آنِفاً (Very close to the present moment; just a moment ago.)  [just now]",
 "いままでで": "حتّى الآن (Until now; until the present time.)  [to date]\nusu. used in superlative clauses together with 一番, 最も, 最悪, etc.\nمثال: 今まででお客は５人だけです。\n→ Up to now, only five guests have arrived.",
 "いままでにない": "غَيْر مَسْبُوق (Never before seen, done, or experienced; without precedent.)  [unprecedented]\nمثال: 彼は今までにないほどに勤勉だ。\n→ He is as diligent a man as ever lived.",
 "いまも": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nمثال: それに関する私の記憶は今も鮮やかに残っている。\n→ My memory of that is still vivid.",
 "いまもって": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]",
 "いまもなお": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]",
 "いまや": "الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now (esp. in contrast to the past)]\nمثال: トムはいまや以前にもまして勤勉に働いている。\n→ Tom works more diligently now.",
 "いまわしい": "بَغِيض (Worthy of, or causing, abhorrence, as a thing of evil omen; odious in the utmost)  [abominable]\nمثال: 考えるだけでも忌まわしい。\n→ The very thought is abhorrent to me. / [ominous ; inauspicious]",
 "いまをさる": "قَبْلَ (Before now, before the present time)  [ago]",
 "いまをさること": "قَبْلَ (Before now, before the present time)  [ago]",
 "いまんとこ": "حَالِيًّا (At this moment, at present, now.)  [currently]",
 "いま一歩": "آخَر, إِضَافِيّ (One more further, in addition to the quantity by then; a second or additional on) / آخَر, أُخْرَى (Not the same; different.)  [another] / [not quite]\nمثال: 監督はチームをトーナメント優勝に今一歩という所までもっていったのに悔しいことだった。\n→ It was annoying, as the manager took his team to a near-miss in the tournament. / [close run ; just falling short of success]",
 "いみ": "مَعْنًى (symbolic value of something) / الْمَعْنَى (symbolic value of something) / مَعْنًى (significance of a thing, as \"the meaning of life\") / مَعْنًى (definition or connotation of a word)  [meaning]\nمثال: その語にはいくつかの意味がある。\n→ The word has several meanings.",
 "いみあい": "تَلَازُم (The connective in propositional calculus that, when joining two predicates A and)  [implication]\nمثال: 私の言いたいことはもっと広い意味合いのものである。\n→ My point is a broader one.",
 "いみありげ": "ذُو مَعْنًى (Having meaning, significant.)  [meaningful]",
 "いみがない": "عَدِيمُ الْفَائِدَةِ (Without use or the possibility to be used.)  [useless]",
 "いみしん": "ذُو مَعْنًى (Having meaning, significant.)  [meaningful]\nمثال: あのドラマ、最後にいつも意味深な言葉を言って終わるよね。\n→ Each episode of that TV drama ends with somebody delivering a profound line.",
 "いみしんちょう": "ذُو مَعْنًى (Having meaning, significant.)  [meaningful]\nمثال: 彼女の態度は意味深長だった。\n→ She gave me a meaningful look.",
 "いみするもの": "مَعْنًى (symbolic value of something) / الْمَعْنَى (symbolic value of something) / مَعْنًى (significance of a thing, as \"the meaning of life\") / مَعْنًى (definition or connotation of a word)  [meaning]\nمثال: このことは彼等が他の諸国民と何も共通点がないことを意味するものではない。\n→ This does not mean that they have nothing in common with other peoples.",
 "いみてき": "دَلَالَات الأَلفَاظ (Of or relating to semantics or the meanings of words.)  [semantic]",
 "いみない": "بدون جدوى (Having no purpose; purposeless; unable to effect an aim.)  [pointless]",
 "いみないよう": "مَعْنًى (symbolic value of something) / الْمَعْنَى (symbolic value of something) / مَعْنًى (significance of a thing, as \"the meaning of life\") / مَعْنًى (definition or connotation of a word)  [meaning (of a sentence)]",
 "いみふ": "غَامِض (Open to multiple interpretations.)  [ambiguous]",
 "いみふめい": "غَامِض (Open to multiple interpretations.)  [ambiguous]\nمثال: 意味不明の微笑が日本人に特有である、としばしば指摘される。\n→ It is often pointed out that a vague smile is typical of the Japanese.",
 "いみぶか": "ذُو مَعْنًى (Having meaning, significant.)  [meaningful]\nمثال: あのドラマ、最後にいつも意味深な言葉を言って終わるよね。\n→ Each episode of that TV drama ends with somebody delivering a profound line.",
 "いみぶかい": "غَنِيّ (having wealth)  [rich (in meaning)]",
 "いみょう": "لَقَب (familiar, invented given name) / كُنْيَة (familiar, invented given name) / اِسْم الدَّلَع (familiar, invented given name)  [nickname]\nمثال: まずいよ。また遅刻だ！！はやくも遅刻魔の異名をとってしまう。\n→ Oh no! I'm late again!! I'm going to get the nickname 'King of Late arrival'.",
 "いみろん": "عِلْم اَلْمَعَانِي (science of the meaning of words)  [semantics]",
 "いみん": "هِجْرَة, مُهَاجَرَة (The act of immigrating; the passing or coming into a country of which one is not)  [immigration]\nمثال: 合衆国は長い間「るつぼ」として知られているが、それは国民のほとんどが移民の子孫だからである。\n→ The United States has long been known as a \"melting pot\" because most of its people are descended from immigrants. / مُهَاجِر, مُهَاجِرَة (A non-native person who comes to a country from another country to permanently s)  [immigrant]\nمثال: ドイツの首相は移民問題に悩まされています。\n→ The German Chancellor is plagued by immigration problems.",
 "いみんだん": "مُهَاجِر, مُهَاجِرَة (Someone who leaves a country to settle in a new country.)  [emigrants]",
