 "いや": "كَرِهَ (To have a feeling of aversion or antipathy towards; not to like.)  [disliking]\nمثال: 彼の話し方が嫌なの。\n→ I don't like his way of talking. / رَهِيب, فَظِيع (Causing horror; terrible; shocking.) / فَظِيع, أَرْبَد (Tremendously bad.)  [horrible]\nمثال: この卵は嫌な匂いがする。\n→ This egg has a bad smell. / [no! ; quit it!]",
 "いやぁ": "وَا, يَا or يَاه (Expression of surprise.) / آه (Expression of understanding, affirmation, recognition, or realization.) / يَا, أَيْ (An invocation or address (similar to the vocative in languages with noun declens)  [oh]\nexpresses surprise or admiration / [well, ... ; er ...]\nمثال: 「どう思う？」「いや、賛成だ」\n→ \"What do you think?\" \"Well, I'm for it.\"",
