 "いやあん": "وَا, يَا or يَاه (Expression of surprise.) / آه (Expression of understanding, affirmation, recognition, or realization.) / يَا, أَيْ (An invocation or address (similar to the vocative in languages with noun declens)  [oh]",
 "いやおうなし": "إِجْبَارِيّ, إِلْزَامِيّ (Required; obligatory; mandatory.)  [compulsory]",
 "いやがおうでも": "طَوْعًا أَوْ كَرْهًا, شاءَ مَن شاءَ وَأَبَى مَن أَبَى (Whether desired or not; without regard for consequences or wishes of those affec)  [willy-nilly]",
 "いやがおうにも": "طَوْعًا أَوْ كَرْهًا, شاءَ مَن شاءَ وَأَبَى مَن أَبَى (Whether desired or not; without regard for consequences or wishes of those affec)  [willy-nilly]\nnon-standard variant of 否が応でも",
 "いやがらせ": "تَحَرُّش (Persistent attacks and criticism causing worry and distress.)  [harassment]\nمثال: 彼女はエレベーターの中で性的いやがらせを受けた。\n→ She was sexually harassed in an elevator.",
 "いやが応にも": "طَوْعًا أَوْ كَرْهًا, شاءَ مَن شاءَ وَأَبَى مَن أَبَى (Whether desired or not; without regard for consequences or wishes of those affec)  [willy-nilly]\nnon-standard variant of 否が応でも",
