 "いやさか": "اِزْدِهَار, رَخَاء (The condition of being prosperous: having good fortune and a fortune.)  [prosperity] / حَظًّا مُوَفَّقًاَ (Used to wish someone good luck.)  [all the best]",
 "いやし": "شِفَاء (An act of healing, as by a faith healer.)  [healing]",
 "いやしい": "مُتَوَاضِع (Having a low position or a low opinion of oneself; not proud, arrogant, or assum) / وضع (To make humble or lowly; to make less proud or arrogant; to make meek and submis)  [humble] / بَذِيء (Debased; uncouth; distasteful; obscene.)  [vulgar]\nمثال: 卑しいことは絶対にしない。\n→ He is above all meanness. / بَالٍ (Of clothing, a place, etc.: unkempt and worn or otherwise in poor condition due )  [shabby] / طَمَّاع, جَشِع (Having greed; consumed by selfish desires.) / شرِه, نهِم (Prone to overeat.)  [greedy]",
 "いやしからぬ": "مُحْتَرَم (Deserving respect.)  [respectable]",
 "いやしくも": "أَيّ (One at all; at least one; at least one kind of; some; a positive quantity of.) / أَيّ (A/an, each or some, no matter its/their identity or nature.) / أَيّ, كُلّ (Any thing(s) or person(s).)  [any]\nمثال: いやしくもやるからには上手くやれ。\n→ If you do it at all, do it well.",
 "いやしけい": "رَاحَة (Contentment, ease.) / جابر (A consolation; something relieving suffering or worry.) / وَاسَى, عَزَّى (To relieve the distress or suffering of; to provide comfort to.)  [comforting]\nمثال: リラックスできる癒し系の音楽をよく聞いている。\n→ I often listen to soothing music in order to relax.",
