 "うなり声": "آهَة, أَنِين (A low, mournful sound uttered in pain or grief.) / تَأَوَّهَ, أَنَّ (To make a groan.)  [groan] / زَمْجَرَة (A deep, rumbling, threatening sound made in the throat by an animal.) / قَرْقَرَة (The rumbling sound made by a human's hungry stomach.) / زَمْجَرَ (To utter a deep guttural sound, as an angry animal; to give forth an angry, grum)  [growl] / هَمْهَمَة (A hummed tune, i.e. created orally with lips closed.) / هَمْهَمَ, دَنْدَنَ (To make a sound from the vocal cords without pronouncing any real words, with on)  [hum (of a machine, power lines, etc.)]",
 "うなる": "آهَة, أَنِين (A low, mournful sound uttered in pain or grief.) / تَأَوَّهَ, أَنَّ (To make a groan.)  [to groan]\nمثال: なにやら唸りながら、ほとばしるパッションをキャンバスにぶつけている！\n→ Groaning strangely she is hurling her overflowing passion onto the canvas! / أَنَّ (To make a loud, deep cry, especially from pain, anger, or other strong emotion.) / قَهْقَهَ (To laugh in a particularly loud manner.) / زَئِير (The cry of the lion.)  [to roar]\nمثال: その犬は小さな男の子に向かって唸った。\n→ The dog growled at a little boy. / هَمْهَمَة (A hummed tune, i.e. created orally with lips closed.) / هَمْهَمَ, دَنْدَنَ (To make a sound from the vocal cords without pronouncing any real words, with on)  [to hum (engine, wind, etc.)] / [to ooh and aah (in admiration)]",
