 "うねくる": "تَعَرَّجَ (To wind or turn in a course or passage)  [to meander]",
 "うねま": "ثَلْم (Any trench, channel, or groove; often found on wood or metal.)  [furrow]",
 "うねり": "رِيح, ريح (One of the four elements of the ancient Greeks and Romans; air.) / لَفَّ (To turn coils (of a cord or something similar) around something.)  [winding] / اِنْتَفَخَ, وَرِمَ (To cause to become bigger.)  [swell (of waves)]\nمثال: 濃霧に加えてうねりも高かった。\n→ In addition to a thick fog, there was a heavy swell.",
 "うねる": "رِيح, ريح (One of the four elements of the ancient Greeks and Romans; air.) / لَفَّ (To turn coils (of a cord or something similar) around something.)  [to wind (of a road, river, etc.)]\nمثال: 川はうねるように平野を流れている。\n→ The river meanders across the plain. / اِنْتَفَخَ, وَرِمَ (To cause to become bigger.)  [to swell]",
 "うのみ": "[swallowing without chewing] / جَرَعَ, بَلَعَ (To cause (food, drink etc.) to pass from the mouth into the stomach; to take int) / جَرْعَة, شَرْبَة (The amount swallowed in one gulp; the act of swallowing.) / سُنُونُو (A small, migratory bird of the Hirundinidae family with long, pointed, moon-shap)  [swallowing (e.g. a story)]\nمثال: 彼の話をうのみにすることはできなかった。\n→ We could not swallow his story.",
 "うのみにする": "جَرَعَ, بَلَعَ (To cause (food, drink etc.) to pass from the mouth into the stomach; to take int) / جَرْعَة, شَرْبَة (The amount swallowed in one gulp; the act of swallowing.) / سُنُونُو (A small, migratory bird of the Hirundinidae family with long, pointed, moon-shap)  [to swallow (e.g. a story)] / [to swallow (food) whole ; to gobble up]",
 "うば": "جَدَّة (A mother of someone's parent.)  [grandmother]\nمثال: 私は祖母が大好きです。\n→ I love my grandmother very much.",
 "うばいあい": "تَهَافَتَ (To struggle eagerly with others for something thrown upon the ground; to go down)  [scramble (for)]",
 "うばいとる": "سَلَبَ, نَهَبَ (To pillage, take or destroy all the goods of, by force (as in war); to raid, sac)  [to plunder]\nمثال: その男は彼女のかばんを奪い取った。\n→ The man robbed her of her bag.",
 "うばう": "أَخَذَ (To get into one's hands, possession, or control, with or without force.) / أَخَذَ بِـ (To receive or accept (something, especially something which was given).) / اِتَّخَذَ (To receive or accept (something, especially something which was given).) / أَخَذَ (To receive or accept (something, especially something which was given).) / أَخَذَ (To grasp or grip.) / اِسْتَغْرَقَ (To fill or require: to last or expend (an amount of time).)  [to take (by force)]\nمثال: その男が私の財布を奪った。\n→ The man robbed me of my purse. / اِتَّسَعَ, اِحْتَوَى (To include so that it no longer has separate existence; to overwhelm; to cause t) / اِمْتَصَ, تَشَرَّبَ (To suck up; to drink in; to imbibe, like a sponge or as the lacteals of the body) / اِحْتَلَّ, شَغَلَ (To engross or engage wholly; to occupy fully.) / اِسْتَنْفَدَ (To occupy or consume time.) / اِسْتَوْعَبَ, وَعَى (To assimilate mentally.) / دَفَعَ, تَحَمَّلَ (To assume or pay for as part of a commercial transaction.)  [to absorb (one's attention)]\nas 心を〜, 目を〜, etc.",
 "うばぐるま": "عَرَبَةْ أَطْفَال (A small vehicle, usually covered, in which a newborn baby is pushed around in a )  [pram]\nمثال: 乳母車で眠っている赤ちゃんは天使のようにかわいい。\n→ The baby sleeping in the baby carriage is as cute as an angel.",
 "うばん": "ويب (Alternative letter-case form of Web: the World Wide Web.)  [web]",
 "うば車": "عَرَبَةْ أَطْفَال (A small vehicle, usually covered, in which a newborn baby is pushed around in a )  [pram]\nمثال: 乳母車で眠っている赤ちゃんは天使のようにかわいい。\n→ The baby sleeping in the baby carriage is as cute as an angel."
}
